      "text": "Cusco to Puno"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b9ad3e14216c2f08",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "ddbabca6ca0e035369eee778c82fcc7750e9c59d0576160c298caf44298f2311",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-mw8xljay-hrdwq6",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, transfer to the bus station and take a tourist bus to Puno. The journey is a full day of sightseeing, with several stops in the Andes.\n\nYour first stop is the village of Andahuaylillas and its Church of San Pedro de Andahuaylillas. Its elaborate paintings have earned it the name “Sistine Chapel of South America”. The church was built in 1631 on the foundations of an older Inca structure. The exterior is modest, while paintings and decorative plasterwork cover the walls and ceilings inside.\n\nNext, visit Raqchi, an archaeological complex at around 3,500 metres above sea level. Its principal building was the Temple of Viracocha, about 92 metres long and 25 metres wide. A total of 22 columns supported the roof.\n\nStop for a buffet lunch in Sicuani, then continue to La Raya Pass at around 4,400 metres and visit the local museum in Pukara. Arrive in Puno at about 18:00. The city sits on Lake Titicaca at around 3,860 metres above sea level. Check in at your hotel."
    },
